1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,067
What if your reflection lived one day ahead?

2
00:00:03,107 --> 00:00:04,431
You brush your teeth,

3
00:00:04,471 --> 00:00:07,613
glance up, and your reflection is already wearing

4
00:00:07,653 --> 00:00:09,431
a party hat and eating cake.

5
00:00:09,471 --> 00:00:10,924
That is tomorrow's you.

6
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,417
Soon it gets useful.

7
00:00:13,457 --> 00:00:15,507
Your reflection holds up a sign:

8
00:00:15,547 --> 00:00:16,944
bus nine will be late.

9
00:00:16,984 --> 00:00:19,100
You leave later, finish your tea,

10
00:00:19,140 --> 00:00:21,256
and still arrive exactly on time.

11
00:00:21,296 --> 00:00:22,824
Smugness level: maximum.

12
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:25,215
Then it gets greedy.

13
00:00:25,255 --> 00:00:27,564
Your reflection waves a lottery ticket.

14
00:00:27,604 --> 00:00:28,829
You copy the numbers,

15
00:00:28,869 --> 00:00:31,359
buy the ticket, and feel like the smartest

16
00:00:31,399 --> 00:00:32,444
person in history.

17
00:00:32,484 --> 00:00:34,010
Hypothetically, of course.

18
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,177
But then you change your mind.

19
00:00:37,217 --> 00:00:39,995
The reflection freezes, scratches its head,

20
00:00:40,035 --> 00:00:41,306
and holds up a sign:

21
00:00:41,346 --> 00:00:42,814
that is not what I did.

22
00:00:42,854 --> 00:00:45,567
Apparently, tomorrow is only a suggestion.

23
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:49,555
You start to notice how tired it looks.

24
00:00:49,595 --> 00:00:51,962
It lives every day before you do,

25
00:00:52,002 --> 00:00:53,785
and never gets surprised.

26
00:00:53,825 --> 00:00:55,681
It holds up one last sign:

27
00:00:55,721 --> 00:00:57,067
I miss not knowing.

28
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:01,215
One morning the sign says something different:

29
00:01:01,255 --> 00:01:02,457
call Grandpa today.

30
00:01:02,497 --> 00:01:03,632
You don't ask why.

31
00:01:03,672 --> 00:01:06,442
You pick up the phone and talk for an hour.

32
00:01:06,482 --> 00:01:08,924
Some forecasts are better as warnings.

33
00:01:10,150 --> 00:01:11,610
Then comes the twist.

34
00:01:11,650 --> 00:01:14,610
The reflection steps out of the mirror and

35
00:01:14,650 --> 00:01:16,110
sits down beside you.

36
00:01:16,150 --> 00:01:17,967
It was never ahead of you.

37
00:01:18,007 --> 00:01:21,539
It was just patiently waiting for you to catch up.

38
00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:25,545
Maybe that's the real thought experiment.

39
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:28,279
The future isn't a prophecy in the glass.

40
00:01:28,319 --> 00:01:30,080
It's someone who loves you,

41
00:01:30,120 --> 00:01:31,480
standing a day ahead,

42
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,881
saying: come on, I saved you a seat.
